==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Etymology 1===
Abbreviation of {{l|nb|du}} {{l|nb|da}}?, directly translated as "you then?".

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|nb|/ˈdʉːdɑ/}}
* {{rhymes|nb|ʉːdɑ}}
* {{hyphenation|nb|d|d}}

====Phrase====
{{head|nb|phrase}}

# {{lb|nb|Internet slang|text messaging}} {{initialism of|nb|[[du]] [[da]]?||and you? what about you?}}
#: ''jeg bare chiller, dd?''
#:: I am just chilling, and you?

=====Usage notes=====
Usage is mostly by teenagers and youth online and in text messaging, most commonly combined with other initialisms from both Norwegian and English.

===Etymology 2===
Abbreviation of {{m|nb|dag|t=day}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|nb|/dɑːɡ/}}
* {{rhymes|nb|ɑːɡ}}
* {{hyphenation|nb|dd}}
* {{homophones|nb|dag}}

====Noun====
{{head|nb|noun}}
# {{abbreviation of|nb|dag|nodot=1|t=day}}, in a two-digit numeric format used for dates
#: {{ux|nb|dd/mm/åååå|dd/mm/yyyy|inline=1}}
#: {{syn|nb|dag}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|nb|mm}}, {{l|nb|åååå}}, {{l|nb|åå}}, {{l|nb|dd/mm/åååå}}

